stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> fresh_state
    fresh_state --> repo_kind
    repo_kind --> probe_kev
    probe_kev --> scope
    probe_kev --> restart_kev
    probe_kev --> kev_missing

    state kev_unavailable {
        restart_kev --> use_jev
        kev_missing --> install_kev
        kev_missing --> use_jev
        install_kev --> use_jev
        use_jev --> user_gate
    }
    restart_kev --> scope
    install_kev --> scope
    use_jev --> scope
    user_gate --> checks_green

    scope --> design_choices
    design_choices --> verified
    verified --> honest_state
    honest_state --> threshold
    threshold --> checks_green
    threshold --> stalled
    stalled --> threshold
    stalled --> config_skip
    config_skip --> checks_green
    checks_green --> reported
    reported --> [*]

    fresh_state    : Re-read the PR with gh pr view --json state,mergedBy,headRefOid and fetch the base branch, then confirm it is still open and nothing changed since your last look
    repo_kind      : Decide whether the PR changes only a configuration repository, such as a skill library, a checklist repo or an agent config repo that pins skills, or whether it changes code, and write that decision down, because it decides whether a stalled Kev gate may be skipped
    probe_kev      : Send one POST to Kev at localhost port 8009 path /v1/systemone with curl -m 90 and check that it answers with HTTP 200 and probabilities
    restart_kev    : Kev is installed but did not answer, so restart it with launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/io.kev.server, read ~/Library/Logs/kev.log, wait for port 8009 and probe it again
    kev_missing    : Kev is not installed, with no io.kev.server launchd agent and no kev checkout, so ask the user whether to install it and wait for their answer
    install_kev    : The user approved the install, so clone github.com/jaredpalmer/kev, start its server on port 8009 as its README describes, register it as the io.kev.server launchd agent and probe it until it answers
    use_jev        : Kev is down, failed to install or the user declined the install, so send the same requests to hosted Jev at openrouter.ai path /api/alpha/decisions with model ~typesafe/jev-latest, and use Jev wherever this checklist says Kev
    user_gate      : No decision model answers, so verify the change end to end, then ask the user for the merge go-or-no-go with the verified state and the outage, and continue only on an explicit yes
    scope          : Ask Kev whether to keep, split or grow the PR, then move every unrelated change into its own PR
    design_choices : Put each non-obvious naming, layout or scope decision to Kev as its own choice question and take the top option, and on a near-tie add verified facts and re-ask instead of asking the user
    verified       : Verify the change end to end in the real runtime by running the tests and the repo CI gates locally, and deploy to a dev environment where the repo requires it
    honest_state   : Build the Kev state from verified facts only, list unverified items plainly, write criteria neutrally, and add no hypothetical facts
    threshold      : Ask Kev for the merge noul, probe one noul per concern, fix the highest first, and re-ask until it reaches 0.8 for your own PR or 0.95 for a colleague PR with your fix PR applied
    stalled        : The score stays below the gate, so create new true facts instead of asking the user, such as fixing the top concern, running more local checks or dry runs, splitting out unrelated changes or verifying an unverified item, then re-ask, and only when nothing is left to try record the open question on the PR with the Kev scores and do other in-scope tasks
    config_skip    : The PR changes only a configuration repository and the Kev score stalled after every true fact was tried, so record the Kev scores and the skip in the PR body and go on to merge. Never take this step for a code change, where the Kev gate always holds
    checks_green   : Get every check green, required or not, and merge without administrator bypass
    reported       : Report every round in the PR body or final summary, with the Kev or Jev scores, or the Kev outage and the user answer when no model answered
